Tenali Rama and the Priceless Gift (Raw Story)

One day, King Krishnadevaraya announced a competition in his court.

He said, “Bring me the most valuable gift, and you will be rewarded.”

All the courtiers began searching for expensive items.

Some brought gold, others brought jewels, and some brought rare treasures.

Tenali Rama came to the court empty-handed.

The courtiers laughed at him.

The king asked, “Tenali, where is your gift?”

Tenali folded his hands and said, “Your Majesty, I have brought you something very special.”

He then bowed and said, “I offer you my loyalty and wisdom. These are more valuable than any treasure.”

The court became silent.

The king smiled and said, “You are right, Tenali. True value does not lie in riches, but in loyalty and wisdom.”

He declared Tenali Rama the winner.

All the courtiers learned an important lesson that day.

💖 Moral:

True value lies in wisdom and loyalty, not in wealth.
